debug('begin add_signature: GL_JOURNAL_IMPORT_PERF');
   l_info('##SHOW_SQL##'):= 'Y';
  add_signature(
      p_sig_repo_id            => '20915',
      p_sig_id                 => 'GL_JOURNAL_IMPORT_PERF',
      p_sig_sql                => 'select 1 from dual',
      p_title                  => 'How to Improve Journal Import Performance',
      p_fail_condition         => 'RS',
      p_problem_descr          => 'Improving Journal Import Performance',
      p_solution               => '<p>The following provides some tips and suggestions which might help to reduce the overall runtime of the Journal Import program:<br><br>

1. Check the following profile options making sure they are NOT checked or enabled, as these can all affect performance:<br>
<blockquote>
    <b>FND: Debug Log Enabled</b><br>
    <b>GL: Debug Mode</b><br>
</blockquote>


2. Check that you do not have the ''<b>Trace</b>''  option checked for the "Journal Import" concurrent program.
<blockquote>
a. You can check this in the Concurrent > Program > Define form, from the System Administrator responsibility.<br>
b. Also, check profile option "Initialization SQL Statement - Custom" from the System Administrator responsibility at any level.
</blockquote>


3. Check your file ''<b>gllacc.lpc</b>'' version:<br>
You can use the following command to verify the file version: <br>
<blockquote>
strings -a $gl_top/bin/GLLEZL |grep ''$header'' | more
</blockquote>

Concider applying the following recommended patches to a test instance incase you are not on the recommended file gllacc.lpc version. <br><br>

<b>Recommended File version:</b>
<blockquote>
for 12.1: gllacc.lpc 120.15.12010000.6 or higher <br>
for 12.2: gllacc.lpc 120.19.12020000.2 or higher
</blockquote>

<b>for 12.1:</b><br>
<blockquote>
Patch {31676877}:R12.GL.B  Consolidate patch for Journal Import <br>
Patch {31830789}:R12.GL.B R12.1 General Ledger Recommended Patch Collection, September 2020
</blockquote>

<b>for 12.2:</b><br>
<blockquote>
Patch {31830859}:R12.GL.C R12.2 General Ledger Recommended Patch Collection, September 2020 <br>
Patch {32230544}:R12.GL.C Journal Import errors out with signal 11 
</blockquote>

4. Development have added hint index(flex_cc GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS_CAT) to the Journal Import code. The index name should be ''<b>GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS_CAT</b>'' and do not use any other name for the concatenated index.  <br>
Refer to the following published Note to automatically create the recommended concatenated index on the GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS and GL_INTERFACE tables.<br>
[2719574.1] Script to Create Dynamically the Recommended Concatenated Indexes GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS_CAT on GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS and GL_INTERFACE_CAT ON GL_INTERFACE <br><br>

5. Are all required <b>init_SID.ora</b> parameters set correctly according to the script in Note 174605.1?<br>
Refer to: [174605.1] - bde_chk_cbo.sql - EBS initialization parameters - Healthcheck<br><br>

6. Ensure you run the following programs on a regular basis; particularly important after any big data load.<br>
a. <br>
- Navigate to the General Ledger Submit Request window.<br>
- Select the "Program - Optimizer" program.<br>
- Enter Yes for Gather Statistics<br><br>

b. <br>
- Navigate to System Administrator responsibility <br>
- Submit Gather Schema Statistics program for "GL" schema at 30% <br><br>

c. <br>
- Gather the stats on the GL_INTERFACE table as follows: <br>
