      p_fail_condition         => 'RS',
      p_problem_descr          => 'Improving Open Period Performance',
      p_solution               => '<p>The following provides some tips and suggestions which might help to reduce the overall runtime of the Open Periods program:<br><br>

1. Check the following profile options making sure they are NOT checked or enabled, as these can all affect performance:<br>
<blockquote>
    <b>FND: Debug Log Enabled</b><br>
    <b>GL: Debug Mode</b><br>
</blockquote>


2. Check that you do not have the ''<b>Trace</b>''  option checked for the "Open Periods" concurrent program.
<blockquote>
a. You can check this in the Concurrent > Program > Define form, from the System Administrator responsibility.<br>
b. Also, check profile option "Initialization SQL Statement - Custom" from the System Administrator responsibility at any level.
</blockquote>

3. Are all required <b>init_SID.ora</b> parameters set correctly according to the script in Note 174605.1?<br>
Refer to: [174605.1] - bde_chk_cbo.sql - EBS initialization parameters - Healthcheck<br><br>

4. Concider applying the following recommended patches to a test instance incase they are not applied. <br><br>

<b>Recommended File version:</b>
<blockquote>
for 12.1: Patch {29487751} and {31830789} <br>
for 12.2: Patch {29487751} and {31830859}
</blockquote>


5. <br>
a. <br>
Verify if you have the profile ''<b>GL: Number of Open Period Workers</b>'' exists on your instance. Otherwise, create a Profile as documented in the following published MOS note:<br>
Refer [437251.1] General Ledger Performance - Open Period Program - GLOOAP <br><br>

b. <br>
Make certain that parallel hint is turned on. Run the following sql <br>
<blockquote>
<i> select min(to_number(value))
from v$parameter where
name = ''cpu_count'' or name = ''parallel_max_servers''; </i>
</blockquote>

c. <br>
Go to System Administrator: Profile : System
Query the Profile "Profile "GL: Number of Open Period Workers" and set the value from ''<b>step#5b</b>'' SQL output <br><br>

d. <br>
Bounce the Apache and Middle-Tier services for the profile changes to take effect. <br><br>

6. Create a GL_CODE_COMBINATIONS_CAT concatenated index.  <br>
Refer [2719574.1] Script to Create Dynamically the Recommended Concatenated Indexes <br><br>

<b>Note:</b> This is a required index, per development, no matter where the performance problem is, as it improves performance for many other GL functionalities as well. <br><br>

